course: dictionary
lesson: 15627
title: Teleport: jumping across space
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Teleport is a verb. To teleport is to move from one place to another instantly, without travelling through the space in between. You will find it in stories, films and video games, where a character jumps across space by magic or super-technology. «Zara pressed the glowing button and teleported to the top of the mountain.» Zara did not walk or climb. She was simply there.
explain: Use the context to check the meaning. The clues are pressed a glowing button and she was at the top straight away. Ask yourself: did she travel through the space in between? She did not, so teleport means jumping there instantly.
explain: Teleport can also be a noun: a teleport is a pad or doorway in a game that sends a player to another place. «Ben stepped onto the teleport and reappeared by the red flag.» Look out for phrases like teleport to, teleport back and teleport pad.
fact: Teleport is a verb: teleport, teleports, teleported, teleporting.
fact: «Teleport» means to move instantly from one place to another, without travelling through the space between.
fact: In games, a teleport is a pad or doorway that sends a player to another place.
fact: Real science has quantum teleportation, but it moves information about tiny particles, not people.
fact: People do not teleport in real life. It only happens in science fiction, games and stories.
exercise: «Mia pressed the button, and in a flash she teleported to the moon.» What does teleported mean? | Jumped very high in the air | Fell asleep and dreamed about the moon | Walked slowly across a field | *Moved to another place instantly, without crossing the space between
exercise: In the game, Sam stepped onto the teleport pad and appeared at the top of the tower. What is a teleport pad? | A pad of paper for drawing | A kind of spaceship engine | A soft mat for jumping on at the gym | *A pad that sends a player to another place
exercise: Which word in «The wizard will teleport the knight back to the castle» is a verb meaning to move instantly? | castle | wizard | knight | *teleport
test: «Scientists say quantum teleportation moves information about tiny particles, not people.» What does this tell you about real teleporting? | Particles are very big | Information is a kind of food | *Real people do not teleport; it only happens in stories and games | Scientists teleport people every day
test: Which sentence uses teleport as a noun, meaning a place or device? | «We will teleport to the park later.» | *«The map has a teleport in the middle, near the blue tower.» | «Please teleport the bag to my room.» | «The hero teleported out of the cave.»
exam: Tom's sister says «I can teleport to school!» What is she probably doing? | *Pretending, as in a story | Flying there in a real plane | Taking a taxi to school | Going to school by bus
